  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN251.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ piriviṉkaṇ vēṟupaṭṭa talaimakaḷatu vēṟupāṭu kaṇṭu tōḻi colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the confidante said upon seeing the changes in HER who had undergone changes during the separation from HIM.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN251.1">
        <l>tūtuñ ceṉṟaṉa tōḷuñ ceṟṟu</l>
        <l>mōti yoṇṇu<supplied>ta</supplied>ṟ pacalaiyu māyum</l>
        <l>vīṅki<supplied>ḻai</supplied> nekiḻac cāayc cellaloṭu</l>
        <l><anchor n="1"/>nāmpaṭar kūru <supplied>maru</supplied>ntuyar kēṭpi</l>
        <l>ṉantaṉ veṟukkai yeytiṉu maṟṟavaṭ</l>
        <l>ṭaṅkalar vāḻi tōḻi velkoṭit</l>
        <l>tuṉaikā laṉṉa puṉaitērk kōcar</l>
        <l>toṉmū tālat tarumpiṇaip potiyi</l>
        <l>liṉṉicai muracaṅ kaṭippikut tiyampat</l>
        <l>temmuṉai citaitta ñāṉṟai mōkūrp</l>
        <l>paṇiyā maiyiṟ pakaitalai vanta</l>
        <l>mākeḻu tāṉai vam<supplied>pa</supplied> mōriyar</l>
        <l>puṉaitēr nēmi yuruḷiya kuṟaitta</l>
        <l>vilaṅkuveḷ ḷaruviya viraivā yumpar</l>
        <l>mācil veṇkōṭ ṭaṇṇal yāṉai</l>
        <l>vāyuṭ ṭappiya varuṅkēḻ vayappuli</l>
        <l>mānila neḷiyak kuttiya pukalvoṭu</l>
        <l>kāmpil vaikun tēkkamal cōlai</l>
        <l>nirampā nīḷiṭaip pōki</l>
        <l>yarampō ḻavvaḷai nilainekiḻt tōrē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1">The messages have gone, [your] shoulders resist,</l>
        <l corresp="2">and the pallor vanishes from [your] bright forehead [surrounded by] hair.</l>
        <l corresp="4">If he hears of the difficult misery when we abound in affliction</l>
        <l corresp="3">together with distress, being emaciated so that [our] copious jewels become loose,</l>
        <l corresp="5a-c">even if he were to obtain the riches of the Nanta [king],</l>
        <l corresp="5d-6c">he would not stay there, oh friend,</l>
        <l corresp="20d">– the one who,</l>
        <l corresp="14">beyond the place where the shining white waterfall rushes</l>
        <l corresp="13">that was checked when the wheels of the decorated chariots rolled over [it],</l>
        <l corresp="12">[the chariots] of the new Maurya with an army having horses</l>
        <l corresp="11">that came in enmity, because of [its] not being humble,</l>
        <l corresp="10">over Mōkūr at the time the hot frontier destroyed [it],</l>
        <l corresp="9">while the sweet-sounding drum sounded, beaten by the drumsticks,</l>
        <l corresp="8">in the public hall with ties difficult [to undo] on the very ancient banyan tree</l>
        <l corresp="6d-7">of the Kōcar with decorated chariots, like the fast wind, with victorious banners,</l>
        <l corresp="19">going the endless long way</l>
        <l>through groves dense with teak trees, where the majestic elephant</l>
        <l corresp="15 18">with flawless white tusks stays among the leaf stems,</l>
        <l corresp="17">with pride as he pierced, so that the dark ground was hollowed,</l>
        <l corresp="16">the lustrous strong tiger from whose maw it is difficult to escape,</l>
        <l rend="indent2" corresp="20">made those saw-cut bangles loose from [their] place.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
